\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{Counting corners with a mass}
\date{2026-11-27}

\p{At trivial links the centered coefficient vanishes at several momenta. Two such zeros can have opposite [local degrees](fdip-013Y). A mass can give opposite signs at the two zeros, so canceling their degrees before reading their masses loses information. Which signed count then distinguishes the mass windows, and how does it enter the index when flux is present?}
